---
import Screenshot from "../Screenshot.astro";
---

<section aria-labelledby="stages-title" class="overflow-hidden border-y border-line bg-subtle py-20 sm:py-28">
  <div class="container-page grid items-center gap-14 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-16">
    <div class="lg:col-span-5">
      <p class="text-eyebrow">Stages and emails</p>
      <h2 id="stages-title" class="text-heading mt-4">Keep candidates in the loop, automatically.</h2>
      <p class="text-lead mt-6">
        Every job has its own stages. Move an applicant to the next one, and that stage's email goes out on its own,
        written once and personal for everyone.
      </p>
      <ul class="check-list mt-8 flex flex-col gap-4 text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed">
        <li>Start with ready-made stages, then rename, reorder, and add your own to fit each role.</li>
        <li>
          Each stage comes with a ready-made email. Personalize it with details like first name and job title, and check
          it in a live preview.
        </li>
        <li>Moved someone by mistake? Undo it, and the email isn't sent.</li>
        <li>Emails use your company's template and logo, and replies go to the address you choose.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- The email as it's written, and as Sam will get it. -->
    <div class="lg:col-span-7">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-xl lg:max-w-none">
        <div class="shot w-[92%]">
          <Screenshot
            name="stage-email"
            alt="The email for the Interviewing stage in Emploist. The subject and message use variables for the applicant's first name, the job title, and the company name."
            sizes="(min-width: 76rem) 39rem, (min-width: 64rem) 52vw, 92vw"
          />
        </div>
        <div class="relative z-10 -mt-10 ml-auto w-[78%] rounded-xl shadow-[var(--shot-shadow)] sm:-mt-16">
          <Screenshot
            name="stage-email-preview"
            alt="The finished email, as an applicant named Sam receives it: Northwind Labs at the top, a personal invitation to interview for the Senior Product Designer role, and a link to open roles."
            sizes="(min-width: 76rem) 33rem, (min-width: 64rem) 44vw, 78vw"
            class="rounded-xl"
          />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
